  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Colleagues and outside customers ask for specific price data, such as historical market data for past years ahead of a meeting or a monthly point price at a pipeline location. The person asked looks the figure up in the price sources, waits when a source such as Gas Daily has not been loaded yet, and replies with the price or a data file and an offer to answer questions.",
    "steps": [
      "A colleague or customer emails asking for index, point or historical price data for given periods.",
      "The recipient checks which source holds the data and whether it has been loaded.",
      "If the data is not yet available, the recipient checks back later.",
      "The recipient extracts the prices and assembles them in a reply or attachment.",
      "The reply is sent with an offer to answer follow-up questions."
    ],
    "approach": "Give requesters self-service access to a standard price lookup or a regularly refreshed price extract covering index, basis, Gas Daily and point prices by month, so routine requests are answered without a manual lookup, and flag when a source has not loaded yet.",
    "rationale": "The requests ask for the same kinds of figures in the same shape. A standard price-data layout lets the person asked fill or forward it quickly, and lets customers see exactly which points and periods are available.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
  "formula": {
